## CLI Diagnostic Commands

The `claude` CLI provides diagnostic commands for debugging agent behavior.

### Environment Inspection

```bash
# Show current CLI configuration
claude --env

# Expected output:
# Model: claude-sonnet-4-20250514
# Provider: anthropic
# API Key: configured (hidden)
# Attribution: enabled
# Debug logging: disabled
```

### Session Listing

```bash
# List recent agent sessions
claude --list

# Expected output:
# ID                          Model                      Status
# bc_abc123...                claude-sonnet-4-20250514   completed
# 507f1f7...                  claude-opus-4-20250514     completed
# def456...                   claude-haiku-3-5           failed
```

### Verbose Output

```bash
# Run agent with verbose debug output
claude --verbose "Explain what tools you have available"

# Run agent with JSON output (machine-readable)
claude --output json "What files do you see in this directory?"

# Run agent with session logging
claude --log /tmp/debug-session.log "Refactor the authentication module"
```

### Debugging Misbehavior

```bash
# Force specific model for debugging
claude --model claude-opus-4-20250514 "Reproduce the issue"

# Force specific provider
claude --provider anthropic "Test with Anthropic"

# Check API connectivity
claude --health
```

